  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "subType": "classFeat",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Once per round, the berserker can attempt a bull rush against one target in place of a melee attack, using his full CMB regardless of the attack it replaces. If the bull rush is successful, the target takes an amount of damage equal to the berserker's Strength modifier and is knocked back as normal. The berserker doesn't move with the target. This bull rush doesn't provoke an attack of opportunity.</p>",
